WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.300
Availability focuses on whether systems are operational and accessible as committed or agreed.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.840
Customers often depend on services being available when needed.

3
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:19.600
Engineering activities such as monitoring, redundancy, backups, disaster recovery planning, capacity management, and incident response all contribute to availability objectives.

4
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.840
Availability is not only about uptime percentages.

5
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:30.780
It is also about planning for failure, detecting issues quickly, communicating clearly, and recovering services within expected timeframes.

6
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:40.820
Strong availability practices help customers trust that the organization can operate reliably, respond to disruptions, and maintain service commitments.
